{
  "title": "WPRM recipes import notes without their parentheses, so the parser reads them as part of the food",
  "description": "WP Recipe Maker pages put an ingredient's note in its own span (.wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes), which the page shows in parentheses: \"3 large eggs (room temperature)\". \
The JSON-LD recipeIngredient that extraction uses flattens it to \"3 large eggs room temperature\". extract/wprm.rs reads the HTML only when the recipe has named ingredient groups. \
The parser then keeps the note in the item, so about 250 pipeline-fixture lines fail to match a food: \"eggs room temperature\" (23), \"brown sugar packed\", \"cream cheese room temperature\", \"unsalted butter cold\", \"lemon juice fresh\", \"water lukewarm\", and others. \
These surfaced when p3-pipeline-ingredient-fixtures-stale-raw-lines refreshed the fixtures. \
The old fixtures came from an extractor that kept the parentheses. \
Likely fix: for every WPRM recipe, build lines from the HTML spans (amount, unit, name, notes), with the notes in parentheses, falling back to JSON-LD when the spans are missing. \
Use the same alignment that recovers group headers. \
Measure with make ingredient-catalog-audit (No supported nutrition match, all three corpora). make pipeline should show raw lines regaining their parentheses in fixtures and snapshots. \
Server-side only (ramekin-core extraction), so no web or iOS change.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "extraction",
    "nutrition",
